  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/crenicichla-notophthalmus-2/",
      "html": "<p>Crenicichla notophthalmus is a dwarf Crenicichla from the Rio Negro near Manaus, described in 1913. It reaches up to 8 cm (females remain smaller). It is a cave breeder with parental care.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/crenicichla-notophthalmus-2/",
      "html": "<p>The genus Crenicichla has about 100 species and is one of the most species-rich cichlid genera. Many forms seen alive do not fit the described species. Manaus is the main market for ornamental fish in Brazil, yet when C. notophthalmus is ordered, C. regani almost always arrives instead.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/crenicichla-notophthalmus-2/",
      "html": "<p>Rio Negro near Manaus, Brazil.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/crenicichla-notophthalmus-2/",
      "html": "<p>Despite their small size, these fish should ideally be kept in aquariums with a floor space of at least 80 x 50 cm.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/crenicichla-notophthalmus-2/",
      "html": "<p>Despite their small size, these cave breeders with parental care really have fire in their bodies.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/crenicichla-notophthalmus-2/",
      "html": "<p>Males (not females) have long, pointed first dorsal fin rays, which is not found elsewhere in the genus. The otherwise identical C. regani lacks this. Females may have one or two eye spots with a cherry-red border in the dorsal fin; this is a variable feature. Females remain smaller than males.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/crenicichla-notophthalmus-2/",
      "html": "<p>Cave breeders with parental care.</p>"
    }
  ],
